{
  "$comment": [
    "The lucide-react import campaign. A RECORD of debt, not an allowlist.",
    "",
    "Every entry is a file that named `lucide-react` directly on 2026-09-05, with the number of",
    "glyph names it took. `check:icon-contract` enforces the difference: a file NOT listed here may",
    "not import the package at all; a listed file may never take more than its recorded count; a",
    "listed file that reaches zero must lose its entry, and the check fails until it does; an entry",
    "for a path that no longer exists fails too, so a rename cannot carry an exemption with it.",
    "When the last entry goes, so does this file.",
    "",
    "And the list is compared against git, not trusted: `checkBacklogDirection` reads the previous",
    "version out of the newest validated ancestor, so a change that adds a file together with its",
    "own entry, or raises a count to match a file it just grew, is refused. A gate must not take",
    "its scope from the branch it is gating.",
    "",
    "The counts here are glyph NAMES, not lines: 110 files, 494 imports (178 files and 800 imports on 2026-09-05, before Phase 7 began draining areas)."
  ],
